# Catch linter errors before finishing

After creating or editing any file, verify lint cleanliness before reporting done. Do not leave the user to discover lint issues in CI or the IDE.

## Checklist

1. Edit files as needed.
2. Run IDE diagnostics (`ReadLints`) on every touched path.
3. If any JS/TS/Vue files changed, also run `npm run lint` and fix every reported problem.
4. If any PHP files changed, run `vendor/bin/pint --dirty --format agent`.
5. Re-check until clean, then summarize for the user.

## Project gotchas

- `package.json` has `"type": "module"`. Do not mix `require()` into ESM configs. For Tailwind, use `tailwind.config.cjs` with `require()` (CommonJS-only plugins/types).
- After config renames, update `components.json` / eslint ignores and confirm lint is clean.
- Pest stubs and Inertia page path casing can pass locally and still fail CI; treat both as required.
- Vue `defineProps` assigned to `props` will fail `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` if you only use the prop in the template — call `defineProps<...>()` without binding, or destructure used fields.
